# reduced from the calt feature of ClimateCrisis (googlefonts/fontc#1849),
# which repeats one of its rules verbatim.
#
# Consecutive rules that share prefix, suffix and lookups are merged into a
# single rule with a wider input position, but the merge must drop duplicate
# glyphs (as fonttools does, by merging into a set): a repeated rule that
# leaves 'i' in the input position twice would make the input look like a
# multi-glyph class, and that would disqualify the whole lookup from format 1,
# which is by far the smallest encoding here.
feature calt {
    sub a a' by A;
    sub b b' by B;
    sub c c' by C;
    sub i i' by I;
    sub i i' by I;
    sub l l' by L;
} calt;
